    TeslaSync.App.UITests.Fixtures.UiAutomationUnavailableException :
      UI automation cannot run: WinAppDriver/Appium runner is absent: nothing is listening on
      http://127.0.0.1:4723/ and WinAppDriver.exe was not found at its standard install paths or on PATH.
  By design (WinAppDriverSession.cs / UiAutomationUnavailableException.cs): when the runner or the deployed
  packaged app is absent, "it is deliberately a hard failure, not an xUnit skip". The UITests project tags
  every test [Trait("Category","UIAutomation")] precisely so the headless unit suite (Category!=UIAutomation)
  and the E2E suite (Category=UIAutomation) run independently. These 147 are shell/auth/accessibility-tree
  E2E tests of the whole app shell; they are unrelated to the FSMStateDiagram surface and require the
  WinAppDriver runner + an interactive desktop session + a deployed MSIX app. No change to this surface can
  satisfy them; on a WinAppDriver-equipped runner the full gate is expected to pass. This matches every
  sibling feature-view gate (e.g. 0204 AppearanceSettings, 0219 ChatMessageItem).

